{
  "file": "module5",
  "page": 74,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        67.39069366455078,
        527.4334106445312,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "conducted in April 2020. Just under 20 000 of these records were used for a matched analysis of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.3970336914062,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "treatment outcomes in children being treated for DR-TB. The paediatric DR-TB IPD included only",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.234130859375,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "seven children aged below 3 years treated with delamanid, 14 children aged 3–6 years, and 69",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        106.99073028564453,
        527.4232788085938,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "children aged 6–12 years. All 21 children aged below 6 years were successfully treated. The number",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        301.5174560546875,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "of children was insufficient for a matched analysis.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.71859741210938,
        527.2315673828125,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "GDG considerations : The GDG noted that when the delamanid phase II trial was started, many of the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 10.975071907043457,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.3990478515625,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "companion drugs in the optimized background regimen were not widely available (such as linezolid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.29469299316406,
        527.4298095703125,
        182.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "and moxifloxacin). By the time the phase III trial started, linezolid and moxifloxacin became more",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.4947052001953,
        527.4247436523438,
        195.9376983642578
      ],
      "text": "accessible, which meant that the optimized background regimens in the trial were likely more effective,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.960077285766602,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69471740722656,
        527.3464965820312,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "making it more difficult to prove the added effect of a drug (i.e. delamanid) in the intervention",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.4367065429688,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "regimen. The GDG concluded that the desirable effects are small. The GDG discussion around the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.09474182128906,
        527.4190063476562,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "undesirable effects focused on adverse events, including those related to the central nervous system",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        234.29469299316406,
        527.3485717773438,
        248.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "and cardiac toxicities, as well as the newly reported adverse event of hallucinations which was of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        247.4947052001953,
        527.4398193359375,
        261.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "some concern to GDG members given the period of dynamic brain development in children. The",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        260.6947021484375,
        527.3934936523438,
        275.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "GDG considered that the risks and benefits (and balance of both) are very different for treating a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        273.89459228515625,
        527.4024658203125,
        288.3376159667969
      ],
      "text": "child with resistant forms of TB (i.e. MDR/RR-TB and XDR-TB) and with limited treatment options,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        287.0947265625,
        527.3903198242188,
        301.5377502441406
      ],
      "text": "compared to a healthy child at future risk of developing MDR-TB (i.e. where delamanid is used for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        300.294677734375,
        527.5455932617188,
        314.7377014160156
      ],
      "text": "prevention). Therefore, the GDG concluded that the balance between desirable and undesirable effects",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.950940132141113,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        313.49468994140625,
        527.1316528320312,
        327.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "probably favours the intervention. The GDG further stated that with the 25 mg dispersible tablet, that",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.988544464111328,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        326.6947021484375,
        527.4089965820312,
        341.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "would be available in the future, the resource implications could vary. Delamanid containing longer",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        339.89471435546875,
        527.59912109375,
        354.3377380371094
      ],
      "text": "treatment regimens were thought to potentially increase equity and be acceptable to stakeholders. In",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.984539031982422,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        353.0946960449219,
        527.2876586914062,
        367.5377197265625
      ],
      "text": "addition, the GDG judged that the use of delamanid in children of all ages would probably be feasible,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.974320411682129,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        366.2947082519531,
        527.413330078125,
        380.73773193359375
      ],
      "text": "especially as the child-friendly formulation of delamanid was expected to become available later in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        379.4947204589844,
        527.4366455078125,
        393.937744140625
      ],
      "text": "2021 (this formulation is now available). This judgement also considered that adult tablets cannot be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        392.6947021484375,
        524.3768310546875,
        407.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "split, crushed or dissolved to ease administration in children without potentially altering bioavailability.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.980833053588867,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        417.67730712890625,
        209.15652465820312,
        433.529296875
      ],
      "text": "Subgroup considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        440.56121826171875,
        527.4160766601562,
        455.18023681640625
      ],
      "text": "Extrapulmonary TB :  The use of delamanid in children with extrapulmonary MDR/RR-TB may be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        453.93719482421875,
        527.1803588867188,
        468.3802185058594
      ],
      "text": "considered (as part of longer regimens used for children with extrapulmonary MDR/RR-TB) by",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        467.13720703125,
        527.4288940429688,
        481.5802307128906
      ],
      "text": "extrapolating data from those with PTB; the delamanid trials, however, have studied PK and safety",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        480.33721923828125,
        278.2228088378906,
        494.7802429199219
      ],
      "text": "among children with pulmonary MDR/RR-TB.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        501.8651428222656,
        527.4351196289062,
        516.484130859375
      ],
      "text": "Children living with HIV :  Children living with HIV were not enrolled in trials 242–12–232 and 233.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        515.2410888671875,
        527.6448364257812,
        529.68408203125
      ],
      "text": "Although evaluated in healthy adult volunteers, reports from antiretroviral drug-drug interaction",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        528.4411010742188,
        527.5838623046875,
        542.8840942382812
      ],
      "text": "studies suggest that the CYP3A4 inhibitor lopinavir/ritonavir increases delamanid total body",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        538.8471069335938,
        527.4154052734375,
        556.0841064453125
      ],
      "text": "(90) exposure up to 25% [GMR: 1.22 (90% CI 1.06,1.40)]  . This increase is not clinically relevant and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        554.8411865234375,
        527.3902587890625,
        569.2841796875
      ],
      "text": "does not necessitate any dose adjustments. No change in delamanid exposure was observed with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        568.0411376953125,
        527.4443969726562,
        582.484130859375
      ],
      "text": "co-administration of either tenofovir [GMR: 0.96 (90% CI 0.84,1.10)], a CYP1A2 inhibitor, or efavirenz",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        581.2410888671875,
        527.4234619140625,
        595.68408203125
      ],
      "text": "[GMR: 0.94 (90% CI 0.72,1.23)], a weak CYP3A4 inducer. Delamanid does not affect plasma exposure",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        591.647216796875,
        527.4082641601562,
        608.8842163085938
      ],
      "text": "(94) of the antiretroviral drugs tenofovir, lopinavir/ritonavir or efavirenz  . No drug interaction studies",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        607.64111328125,
        527.2474975585938,
        622.0841064453125
      ],
      "text": "of delamanid together with integrase inhibitors have been performed, but based on knowledge",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        618.047119140625,
        527.4215698242188,
        635.2841186523438
      ],
      "text": "(95) of metabolic pathways, the risk of metabolic drug interaction potential is expected to be low  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        634.0411376953125,
        527.4287719726562,
        648.484130859375
      ],
      "text": "Therefore, based on available evidence, delamanid can be given to CLHIV with MDR/RR-TB on ART",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        647.2410888671875,
        234.84420776367188,
        661.68408203125
      ],
      "text": "regimen without dose adjustments.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        672.2236938476562,
        245.23455810546875,
        688.0757446289062
      ],
      "text": "Implementation considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        695.2835693359375,
        527.4487915039062,
        709.7265625
      ],
      "text": "Delamanid has been in use for adults and adolescents since 2014 and for children since 2016 (from",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        708.4835815429688,
        527.4100952148438,
        722.9265747070312
      ],
      "text": "6 years of age) and 2019 (from 3 years) and therefore the implementation considerations related",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        721.68359375,
        527.4530029296875,
        736.1265869140625
      ],
      "text": "to its use in children below 3 years of age are an extension of those currently in place. The main",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        734.8837280273438,
        527.5847778320312,
        749.3267211914062
      ],
      "text": "implementation considerations specifically applicable to this age group are dosing based on the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        748.0836791992188,
        463.0789489746094,
        762.5266723632812
      ],
      "text": "availability of the 25 mg dispersible formulation and the neuropsychiatric side effects.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        41.23320007324219,
        801.0170288085938,
        136.43409729003906,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "50 WHO consolidated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        136.43649291992188,
        801.0170288085938,
        170.0604705810547,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "guidelines",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        170.06539916992188,
        801.0170288085938,
        450.3536071777344,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "on tuberculosis, Module 5: Management of tuberculosis in children and adolescents",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}